{"node":{"id":"MONDO:0008998","label":"Cockayne syndrome type 3","definition":"Cockayne syndrome type III, also known as the mild form of Cockayne syndrome, is a rare genetic disorder that causes early (premature) aging. Unlike the more severe forms of this condition, individuals with Cockayne syndrome type III can have normal growth and development. Symptoms may include sunlight sensitivity (photosensitivity), hearing loss, eye and bone abnormalities, and changes to the brain that can be seen on imaging (brain MRIs). In general, symptoms of Cockayne syndrome type III are usually not noticeable until later in childhood.","synonyms":["Cockayne syndrome type C","Cockayne syndrome type III"],"xrefs":["GARD:0001417","MEDGEN:196713","OMIM:216411","Orphanet:90324","UMLS:C0751037","icd11.foundation:1401163130"],"parents":["MONDO:0016006"],"parents_labels":{"MONDO:0016006":"Cockayne syndrome"},"children":[],"children_labels":{},"in_core":false,"cluster_id":6,"is_group":false,"n_genes":2,"n_phenotypes":74,"mechanism_classes":[]},"genes":[{"id":"e_ea5b2be4c126","source":"MONDO:0008998","target":"ERCC6","type":"caused_by","evidence":[{"db":"Orphanet","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:90324","level":"curated","date":"2026-06-23","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/90324","confidence":0.95,"snippet":"Disease-causing germline mutation(s) (loss of function) in (Assessed) — ERCC excision repair 6, chromatin remodeling factor"},{"db":"HPO","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:90324","level":"curated","date":"2026-09-02","confidence":0.9,"url":"https://hpo.jax.org/browse/disease/ORPHA:90324","snippet":"ERCC6 is annotated as disease gene of ORPHA:90324 (HPO genes_to_phenotype, Orphanet-derived)"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":0.95,"independent_sources":["Orphanet"],"level":"curated"},{"id":"e_96d311ea0305","source":"MONDO:0008998","target":"ERCC8","type":"caused_by","evidence":[{"db":"Orphanet","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:90324","level":"curated","date":"2026-06